<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "container.hub">
<!ENTITY author    "LX-S93">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.11.06.5">
<!ENTITY md5       "11d3aa2a1dda5cdc443bf2b89c91026a">
<!ENTITY github    "LX-S93/unraid-container-hub">
<!ENTITY gitURL    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&github;/main">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "&gitURL;/&name;.plg">
<!ENTITY pkg       "&name;-&version;-x86_64-1">
<!ENTITY cfg       "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
]>
<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" support="https://github.com/&github;/issues" project="https://github.com/&github;" min="7.0.0" icon="cubes" launch="Docker">

<CHANGES>
### 2026.11.06.5
- Container Hub now lives inside the Docker tab instead of its own CONTAINERS tab
- The classic container list stays one click away ("Classic view" / "Container Hub" in the title bar)
### 2026.11.06.4
- Details panel slides in over the page again, now resizable by dragging its left edge
### 2026.11.06.3
- Groups stand out: separate framed blocks with a coloured header bar, larger name and container count
### 2026.11.06.2
- The list is the main view now, grouped by folder/network/compose with collapsible groups (cards view removed)
- Updates stand out: blue Update button per container, marker on the icon, "n updates" per group, filter by updates
- Details panel is docked next to the list instead of covering it, and can be resized by dragging its edge
- Built-in console tab (docker exec) in the details panel
### 2026.11.06.1
- Generic base images (python, node, alpine …) are never used as a logo match
- Cleaner logo rows, alerts and network entries; memory bar only where a limit is set
### 2026.11.06
- First release: a modern Containers page next to the Docker tab
- Cards, list and network views, status overview with "needs attention", details panel with logs
- Uses Unraid's own start/stop, update, console and autostart functions; reads Folder View folders
- Automatic logos from dashboard-icons and selfh.st, optional write-back into the Unraid templates
</CHANGES>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
mkdir -p &cfg;
find &cfg; -maxdepth 1 -name '&name;-*.txz' ! -name '&pkg;.txz' -delete
true
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&cfg;/&pkg;.txz" Run="upgradepkg --install-new">
<URL>&gitURL;/archive/&pkg;.txz</URL>
<MD5>&md5;</MD5>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
echo ""
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo " &name; &version; installed"
echo " Open the DOCKER tab in the top bar"
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
removepkg &pkg; >/dev/null 2>&amp;1
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name; /tmp/&name;
rm -f &cfg;/&name;-*.txz
echo "&name; removed. Settings, logos and template backups are kept in &cfg;"
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
